{"units": [{"id": "poios-word13", "translation": "With what spirit of the Pelasgian men do you dishonor this woman?"}, {"id": "poios-word14", "translation": "of what kind?"}, {"id": "poios-word15", "translation": "of whom?"}, {"id": "poios-word16", "translation": "of whom?"}, {"id": "poios-word17", "translation": "Having said to what kind of protectors?"}, {"id": "poios-word18", "translation": "What pair is this?"}, {"id": "poios-word19", "translation": "the"}, {"id": "poios-word20", "translation": "He has spoken to us, with what charge did Zeus seize you?"}, {"id": "poios-word21", "translation": "And I will teach your father"}, {"id": "poios-word22", "translation": "from the apograph before τοῖα"}, {"id": "poiphygma-orth1", "translation": "violent blowing, sobbing"}, {"id": "poiphygma-def1", "translation": "violent blowing, sobbing"}, {"id": "poiphygma-note1", "translation": "Ἐν ματαίοις κἀγρίοις [in vain and wild things]"}, {"id": "poiphygma-note2", "translation": "Schol. οἷον ἐκφοβήμασι τοῖς δυναμένοις ἐκπλῆξαι τοὺς ἀκούοντας [such as with terrifying things able to astound the hearers]"}, {"id": "poiphygma-quote1", "translation": "with violent blowings"}, {"id": "poiphygma-word1", "translation": "in vain and wild things"}, {"id": "poiphygma-word2", "translation": "such as with terrifying things able to astound the hearers"}, {"id": "polemarchos-orth1", "translation": "leader in war"}, {"id": "polemarchos-def1", "translation": "leader in war"}, {"id": "polemarchos-note1", "translation": "Ἀτέκνους κλαύσω [I will weep for the childless]"}, {"id": "polemarchos-note2", "translation": "Ἀχαιῶν [of the Achaeans]"}, {"id": "polemarchos-quote1", "translation": "leaders in war?"}, {"id": "polemarchos-quote2", "translation": "a man who is a leader in war"}, {"id": "polemarchos-word1", "translation": "I will weep for the childless"}, {"id": "polemarchos-word2", "translation": "of the Achaeans"}, {"id": "polemios-orth1", "translation": "hostile"}, {"id": "polemios-def1", "translation": "hostile"}, {"id": "polemios-def2", "translation": "οἱ πολέμιοι [the enemy] in the verse of an interpolator"}, {"id": "polemios-note1", "translation": "Πολέμιον [hostile]"}, {"id": "polemios-note2", "translation": "Λύουσα [releasing]"}, {"id": "polemios-note3", "translation": "πολεμίων [of enemies] apogr."}, {"id": "polemios-note4", "translation": "Πολεμίους ἐπ᾽ ἀσπίδων [enemies upon shields]"}, {"id": "polemios-note5", "translation": "Πολεμίας ἐπ᾽ [hostile upon]"}, {"id": "polemios-note6", "translation": "Κεκευθώς [having hidden]"}, {"id": "polemios-note7", "translation": "Πῶς ἂν οὖν μένοιεν ἄν-δρας [How then could they await men]"}, {"id": "polemios-note8", "translation": "Δωμάτων κύνα ἐσθλὴν ἐκείνῳ [a noble dog of the house for him]"}, {"id": "polemios-note9", "translation": "Πολεμίων δ᾽ [and of enemies]"}, {"id": "polemios-quote1", "translation": "spear"}, {"id": "polemios-quote2", "translation": "hostile fear"}, {"id": "polemios-quote3", "translation": "gods"}, {"id": "polemios-quote4", "translation": "of a shield"}, {"id": "polemios-quote5", "translation": "from hostile ground"}, {"id": "polemios-quote6", "translation": "hostile invaders?"}, {"id": "polemios-quote7", "translation": "hostile to the ill-minded"}, {"id": "polemios-quote8", "translation": "garments"}, {"id": "polemios-word1", "translation": "hostile"}, {"id": "polemios-word2", "translation": "releasing"}, {"id": "polemios-word3", "translation": "of enemies"}, {"id": "polemios-word4", "translation": "enemies upon shields"}, {"id": "polemios-word5", "translation": "hostile upon"}, {"id": "polemios-word6", "translation": "having hidden"}, {"id": "polemios-word7", "translation": "How then could they await men"}, {"id": "polemios-word8", "translation": "a noble dog of the house for him"}, {"id": "polemios-word9", "translation": "the enemy"}, {"id": "polemios-word10", "translation": "and of enemies"}, {"id": "polemokrantos-orth1", "translation": "accomplished by war"}, {"id": "polemokrantos-def1", "translation": "accomplished by war"}, {"id": "polemokrantos-note1", "translation": "Πολεμόκραντον ἁγνὸν τέλος ἐν [a holy end accomplished by war in]"}, {"id": "polemokrantos-note2", "translation": "Σιμιλε εστ μοιρόκραντος Χη. 612. Ευμ. 392. Νευτρυμ βοχαβυλυμ apud αλιός λεγιτυρ. [Similarly it is μοιρόκραντος [fated] Cho. 612. Eum. 392. Neuter vocabuli apud alios legitur.]"}, {"id": "polemokrantos-quote1", "translation": "in battle"}, {"id": "polemokrantos-word1", "translation": "a holy end accomplished by war in"}, {"id": "polemokrantos-word2", "translation": "Similarly it is μοιρόκραντος [fated] Cho. 612. Eum. 392. Neuter vocabuli"}, {"id": "polemokrantos-word3", "translation": "apud alios legitur"}, {"id": "polemos-orth1", "translation": "war"}, {"id": "polemos-def1", "translation": "war"}, {"id": "polemos-note1", "translation": "Ἀπόλεμος ὅδε γ᾽ ὁ [This one is unwarlike]"}, {"id": "polemos-note2", "translation": "Καλῶς τὰ πλείω [the greater part well]"}, {"id": "polemos-note3", "translation": "Πολέμου στῖφος [the mass of war]"}, {"id": "polemos-note4", "translation": "Ἐπέσκηψεν δὲ Πέρσαις [and it fell upon the Persians]"}, {"id": "polemos-note5", "translation": "Νόστοι δ᾽ ἐκ πολέμων ἀπόνους, ἀπαθεῖς ἄγον [and returns from wars brought them without toil, unharmed]"}, {"id": "polemos-note6", "translation": "Θεότρε-πτα τάδ᾽ αὐ φέρομεν [we bear these things turned by the gods]"}, {"id": "polemos-note7", "translation": "Γυναικοποίνων [avenging women]"}, {"id": "polemos-note8", "translation": "Θυραῖος ἔστω [let him be outside the door]"}, {"id": "polemos-note9", "translation": "Κἀκ πολέμου [and from war]"}, {"id": "polemos-note10", "translation": "Σικ ρεχτε Ροβορτελλυς προ πτολέμου, θυα φορμα τραγικι νον συντ υσιδεν νισι μετρο ποστυλαντε. [Thus rightly Robortellus for πτολέμου, which tragic form is not used except when the meter demands.]"}, {"id": "polemos-note11", "translation": "Πόλεμον [war]"}, {"id": "polemos-note12", "translation": "Ἡ τοῖσιν ἢ τοῖς πόλεμον αἴρεσθαι μέγαν πᾶσ᾽ ἔστ᾽ [It is possible for all to raise great war either against these or those]"}, {"id": "polemos-note13", "translation": "Πολέμους θ᾽ [and wars]"}, {"id": "polemos-quote1", "translation": "war"}, {"id": "polemos-quote2", "translation": "war comes from the gods"}, {"id": "polemos-quote3", "translation": "providing"}, {"id": "polemos-quote4", "translation": "to conduct wars that destroy towers"}, {"id": "polemos-quote5", "translation": "houses"}, {"id": "polemos-quote6", "translation": "in wars"}, {"id": "polemos-quote7", "translation": "aid of wars"}, {"id": "polemos-quote8", "translation": "war"}, {"id": "polemos-quote9", "translation": "to those being worn down"}, {"id": "polemos-quote10", "translation": "to raise new"}, {"id": "polemos-quote11", "translation": "necessity"}, {"id": "polemos-quote12", "translation": "I fear bloody ones"}, {"id": "polemos-word1", "translation": "This one is unwarlike"}, {"id": "polemos-word2", "translation": "the greater part well"}, {"id": "polemos-word3", "translation": "the mass of war"}, {"id": "polemos-word4", "translation": "and it fell upon the Persians"}, {"id": "polemos-word5", "translation": "and returns from wars brought them without toil, unharmed"}, {"id": "polemos-word6", "translation": "we bear these things turned by the gods"}, {"id": "polemos-word7", "translation": "avenging women"}, {"id": "polemos-word8", "translation": "let him be outside the door"}, {"id": "polemos-word9", "translation": "and from war"}, {"id": "polemos-word10", "translation": "Thus rightly Robortellus for πτολέμου, which tragic form is not used except when the meter demands"}, {"id": "polemos-word11", "translation": "war"}, {"id": "polemos-word12", "translation": "It is possible for all to raise great war either against these or those"}, {"id": "polemos-word13", "translation": "and wars"}, {"id": "polemophthoros-orth1", "translation": "destroying in war"}, {"id": "polemophthoros-def1", "translation": "destroying in war"}, {"id": "polemophthoros-note1", "translation": "Οὐδὲ γὰρ ἄνδρας ποτ᾿ ἀπώλλυ [For he never destroyed men]"}, {"id": "polemophthoros-quote1", "translation": "with destructive follies of war"}, {"id": "polemophthoros-word1", "translation": "For he never destroyed men"}, {"id": "poleo-orth1", "translation": "to turn"}, {"id": "poleo-def1", "translation": "to turn"}, {"id": "poleo-def2", "translation": "Passive with these, Homeric form written with w"}, {"id": "poleo-note1", "translation": "Euripides used it intransitively"}, {"id": "poleo-note2", "translation": "Τί σὺ τῇδε [Why do you ... here?]"}, {"id": "poleo-note3", "translation": "Ετ χυμ ἀμφί [and with ... around]"}, {"id": "poleo-note4", "translation": "εν θυο νιηιλ εστ ινσολιτι: μιρε βερο χυμ αχχυσατιβο σινε πραεπο-σιτιον χονστρυχιτ Αεσχυλους φρεθυεντανδι σενσυ [in two places it is unusual: remarkably, Aeschylus constructs it with an accusative without a preposition in a frequentative sense]"}, {"id": "poleo-note5", "translation": "Τενάγων νῆσον Αἴαντος [the island of Ajax, Tenagos]"}, {"id": "poleo-note6", "translation": "Ὄψεις ἔννυχοι [nightly visions]"}, {"id": "poleo-note7", "translation": "where in the Mam. recension πο is written above, in several apographs πολούμεναι is placed. πωλεύμεναι is said after the example of Homer, Od."}]}